pub(crate) fn print_logs_help() {
    println!(
        "Usage: phasegent logs [--run ID] [--limit N] [--path]\n\nRead-only view of the bounded diagnostic log that `worktree prune` leaves by default (no debug flag, no configuration, no provider, no credential, and no registry). The log records typed metadata only: no path, no session or issue identifier, no credential, no URL, no request or response body, and no raw error text. It is diagnostic evidence, never an authority: no guard reads it and no log line authorizes a removal.\n\n--run ID returns the events of exactly that run; the identifier is 1..128 characters of letters, digits, '.', '_', ':', or '-'. --limit N returns at most N events, 1..500, default 50; the newest matching events are returned in chronological order. --path reports the resolved log directory and its fixed retention limits without reading or creating anything; it cannot be combined with --run or --limit.\n\nThe directory is the platform state directory when there is one and the local application data directory otherwise: ~/.local/state/phasegent/logs on Linux, ~/Library/Application Support/com.Cloud1ful.phasegent/logs on macOS, and %LOCALAPPDATA%\\Cloud1ful\\phasegent\\data\\logs on Windows. It holds the active NDJSON file prune.jsonl, the archives prune.jsonl.1 to prune.jsonl.4, and the stable lock file prune.log.lock. Every file is at most 2 MiB, so the whole set stays within 10 MiB; the active file rolls over when the next event would exceed the cap or when it was last written on an earlier UTC day, and an owned file older than 14 days is deleted when a writer starts. The files are private (0600, in a 0700 directory).\n\nThe query reads only those owned files, takes the shared lock without waiting, and reports the directory, the retention limits, the events, how many lines were skipped as malformed, and whether a writer held the lock. A busy lock yields empty entries and busy=true; no logs at all is an empty success. A query never writes, never rotates, and never deletes.\n\nLogging is best effort: when the lock is busy or the log cannot be written, the event is dropped and one bounded warning is reported; the prune run itself is never affected."
    );
}
